  "id": "COMPOUND:16267 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Isotrifoliol appears to be a potential activator of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through a shared target, C-C motif chemokine 8. This chemokine is targeted by multiple compounds, including Ganoderic Acid C6 and Decaturin B, which in turn interact with ATR. The evidence suggests that Isotrifoliol may exert its effects by binding to C-C motif chemokine 8, thereby initiating a signaling cascade that ultimately involves Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR. The consistent presence of C-C motif chemokine 8 as a common target across different compounds supports the hypothesis that Isotrifoliol may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of ATR. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of C-C motif chemokine 8 as a central mediator in the interaction between Isotrifoliol and ATR, underscoring the importance of this chemokine in the drug's biological effects.",
